    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 📊 Linear & Polynomial Regression with Statsmodels\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** Implement Linear and Polynomial Regression with full statistical diagnostics.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning Objectives\n",
        "1. Use `statsmodels.OLS` for statistical inference\n",
        "2. Apply `PolynomialFeatures` for non-linear relationships\n",
        "3. Perform proper train/test splitting and evaluation\n",
        "4. Run assumption diagnostics (normality, homoscedasticity)\n",
        "5. Visualize residuals and model fit\n",
        "6. Interpret the full summary table\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why Statsmodels over NumPy?\n",
        "\n",
        "| Feature | NumPy | Statsmodels |\n",
        "|---------|-------|-------------|\n",
        "| Coefficients | ✓ | ✓ |\n",
        "| P-values | ✗ | ✓ |\n",
        "| Confidence intervals | ✗ | ✓ |\n",
        "| R², Adjusted R² | Manual | Automatic |\n",
        "| F-test, t-test | ✗ | ✓ |\n",
        "| Residual diagnostics | ✗ | ✓ |\n",
        "| AIC/BIC | ✗ | ✓ |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Step 1: Import Libraries\n",
        "\n",
        "| Library | Purpose |\n",
        "|---------|--------|\n",
        "| `pandas` | Data loading |\n",
        "| `numpy` | Array operations |\n",
        "| `statsmodels.api` | OLS model, `add_constant` |\n",
        "| `sklearn.preprocessing` | `PolynomialFeatures` |\n",
        "| `sklearn.model_selection` | `train_test_split` |\n",
        "| `sklearn.metrics` | `mean_squared_error` |\n",
        "| `scipy.stats` | Diagnostic tests |\n",
        "| `matplotlib.pyplot` | Visualization |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeatures\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## Step 2: Define the `LinearRegressionStatsmodels` Class\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a reusable wrapper class that provides:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Method | Purpose |\n",
        "|--------|---------|\n",
        "| `prepare_features()` | Add constant and optional polynomial terms |\n",
        "| `fit()` | Fit the OLS model |\n",
        "| `predict()` | Make predictions on new data |\n",
        "| `evaluate()` | Return RMSE, MAE, R² dictionary |\n",
        "| `check_assumptions()` | Run diagnostic tests on residuals |\n",
        "| `plot_residuals()` | Visualize residual diagnostics |\n",
        "| `print_summary()` | Print the full statsmodels summary table |\n",
        "| `get_coefficients()` | Return a clean DataFrame of coefficients |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Design Decisions\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **PolynomialFeatures is optional** — controlled by `add_polynomial` parameter\n",
        "2. **NaN handling** — rows with missing values are dropped before fitting\n",
        "3. **Feature naming** — automatic generation for polynomial terms\n",
        "4. **Diagnostics** — Shapiro-Wilk test for normality, residual visualization"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class LinearRegressionStatsmodels:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    A reusable Linear/Polynomial Regression wrapper around statsmodels.OLS\n",
        "    with built-in diagnostics and evaluation.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        add_polynomial (bool): If True, expand features to degree `degree`\n",
        "        degree (int): Polynomial degree (used only if add_polynomial=True)\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __init__(self, add_polynomial=False, degree=2):\n",
        "        self.add_polynomial = add_polynomial\n",
        "        self.degree = degree\n",
        "        self.results = None\n",
        "        self.model = None\n",
        "        self.feature_names = None\n",
        "        self.poly_transformer = None\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Initialize polynomial transformer if needed\n",
        "        if add_polynomial:\n",
        "            self.poly_transformer = PolynomialFeatures(degree=degree, include_bias=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # FEATURE PREPARATION\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def prepare_features(self, X, is_training=False):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Prepare features: optional polynomial expansion + add constant.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Parameters:\n",
        "            X: pd.DataFrame or np.ndarray\n",
        "            is_training (bool): If True, fit the polynomial transformer.\n",
        "                                If False, only transform (use for test/new data).\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Convert to numpy if DataFrame\n",
        "        if isinstance(X, pd.DataFrame):\n",
        "            self.feature_names = list(X.columns)\n",
        "            X_values = X.values\n",
        "        elif isinstance(X, pd.Series):\n",
        "            self.feature_names = [X.name]\n",
        "            X_values = X.values.reshape(-1, 1)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            X_values = np.array(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Apply polynomial transformation if enabled\n",
        "        if self.add_polynomial and self.poly_transformer is not None:\n",
        "            if is_training:\n",
        "                X_values = self.poly_transformer.fit_transform(X_values)\n",
        "                self.feature_names = self.poly_transformer.get_feature_names_out(self.feature_names)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                X_values = self.poly_transformer.transform(X_values)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Add constant for statsmodels OLS (intercept term)\n",
        "        X_with_const = sm.add_constant(X_values)\n",
        "        return X_with_const\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # MODEL FITTING\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def fit(self, X, y):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Fit the OLS model.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Parameters:\n",
        "            X: Features (pd.DataFrame or np.ndarray)\n",
        "            y: Target (pd.Series or np.ndarray)\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Prepare features (fit polynomial if enabled)\n",
        "        X_prepared = self.prepare_features(X, is_training=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Convert y to numpy if needed\n",
        "        if isinstance(y, pd.Series):\n",
        "            y = y.values\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Drop rows with NaN values\n",
        "        mask = ~np.isnan(X_prepared).any(axis=1) & ~np.isnan(y)\n",
        "        X_clean = X_prepared[mask]\n",
        "        y_clean = y[mask]\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Fit the model\n",
        "        self.results = sm.OLS(y_clean, X_clean).fit()\n",
        "        self.model = self.results.model\n",
        "\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # PREDICTION\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def predict(self, X):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Make predictions on new data.\"\"\"\n",
        "        X_prepared = self.prepare_features(X, is_training=False)\n",
        "        return self.results.predict(X_prepared)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # EVALUATION\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def evaluate(self, y_true, y_pred, label=''):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Calculate and display evaluation metrics.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns: dict with mse, rmse, mae, r2\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        if isinstance(y_true, pd.Series):\n",
        "            y_true = y_true.values\n",
        "\n",
        "        mse = np.mean((y_true - y_pred) ** 2)\n",
        "        rmse = np.sqrt(mse)\n",
        "        mae = np.mean(np.abs(y_true - y_pred))\n",
        "\n",
        "        ss_res = np.sum((y_true - y_pred) ** 2)\n",
        "        ss_tot = np.sum((y_true - np.mean(y_true)) ** 2)\n",
        "        r2 = 1 - (ss_res / ss_tot) if ss_tot != 0 else 0\n",
        "\n",
        "        metrics = {'mse': mse, 'rmse': rmse, 'mae': mae, 'r2': r2}\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Pretty print\n",
        "        if label:\n",
        "            print(f\"\\n--- {label} ---\")\n",
        "            print(f\"  MSE:  {mse:>12.4f}\")\n",
        "            print(f\"  RMSE: {rmse:>12.4f}\")\n",
        "            print(f\"  MAE:  {mae:>12.4f}\")\n",
        "            print(f\"  R²:   {r2:>12.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        return metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # ASSUMPTION DIAGNOSTICS\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def check_assumptions(self, y_true, y_pred):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Run diagnostic tests for OLS assumptions:\n",
        "        1. Linearity (correlation of residuals with predictions)\n",
        "        2. Normality of residuals (Shapiro-Wilk test)\n",
        "        3. Homoscedasticity (visual flag)\n",
        "        4. Independence (Durbin-Watson from model results)\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        if isinstance(y_true, pd.Series):\n",
        "            y_true = y_true.values\n",
        "\n",
        "        residuals = y_true - y_pred\n",
        "\n",
        "        print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n",
        "        print(\"         OLS ASSUMPTION DIAGNOSTICS\")\n",
        "        print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # 1. LINEARITY: Residuals should not correlate with predictions\n",
        "        if np.std(residuals) > 0 and np.std(y_pred) > 0:\n",
        "            corr = np.corrcoef(y_pred, residuals)[0, 1]\n",
        "            status = \"✓ PASS\" if abs(corr) < 0.1 else \"⚠ CHECK\"\n",
        "            print(f\"\\n1. Linearity\")\n",
        "            print(f\"   Correlation(pred, resid) = {corr:.4f}\")\n",
        "            print(f\"   Status: {status} (should be near 0)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # 2. NORMALITY: Shapiro-Wilk test on residuals\n",
        "        if len(residuals) <= 5000:\n",
        "            stat, p_value = stats.shapiro(residuals)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            # Use Anderson-Darling for larger samples\n",
        "            result = stats.anderson(residuals, dist='norm')\n",
        "            p_value = result.significance_level[2] / 100  # Approximate\n",
        "            stat = result.statistic\n",
        "\n",
        "        status = \"✓ PASS\" if p_value > 0.05 else \"⚠ FAIL (residuals not normal)\"\n",
        "        print(f\"\\n2. Normality of Residuals\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Shapiro-Wilk p-value = {p_value:.6f}\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Status: {status} (>0.05 needed)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # 3. HOMOSCEDASTICITY: Breusch-Pagan test (if available)\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            from statsmodels.stats.diagnostic import het_breuschpagan\n",
        "            bp_stat, bp_p, _, _ = het_breuschpagan(residuals, self.results.model.exog)\n",
        "            status = \"✓ PASS\" if bp_p > 0.05 else \"⚠ FAIL (heteroscedasticity)\"\n",
        "            print(f\"\\n3. Homoscedasticity\")\n",
        "            print(f\"   Breusch-Pagan p-value = {bp_p:.6f}\")\n",
        "            print(f\"   Status: {status} (>0.05 needed)\")\n",
        "        except Exception:\n",
        "            print(f\"\\n3. Homoscedasticity\")\n",
        "            print(f\"   ⚠ Check residual plot visually for funnel pattern\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # 4. INDEPENDENCE: Durbin-Watson statistic\n",
        "        dw = sm.stats.durbin_watson(residuals)\n",
        "        status = \"✓ PASS\" if 1.5 < dw < 2.5 else \"⚠ CHECK (possible autocorrelation)\"\n",
        "        print(f\"\\n4. Independence\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Durbin-Watson = {dw:.4f}\")\n",
        "        print(f\"   Status: {status} (ideal ≈ 2.0)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # RESIDUAL PLOTS\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def plot_residuals(self, y_true, y_pred):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Create diagnostic residual plots.\"\"\"\n",
        "        if isinstance(y_true, pd.Series):\n",
        "            y_true = y_true.values\n",
        "\n",
        "        residuals = y_true - y_pred\n",
        "\n",
        "        fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Plot 1: Residuals vs Predicted\n",
        "        axes[0, 0].scatter(y_pred, residuals, alpha=0.5, edgecolors='k')\n",
        "        axes[0, 0].axhline(0, color='red', linestyle='--', lw=2)\n",
        "        axes[0, 0].set_xlabel('Predicted Values')\n",
        "        axes[0, 0].set_ylabel('Residuals')\n",
        "        axes[0, 0].set_title('Residuals vs Predicted\\n(Homoscedasticity check)')\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Plot 2: Q-Q Plot for normality\n",
        "        sm.qqplot(residuals, line='45', fit=True, ax=axes[0, 1])\n",
        "        axes[0, 1].set_title('Q-Q Plot\\n(Normality check)')\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Plot 3: Histogram of residuals\n",
        "        axes[1, 0].hist(residuals, bins=30, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7, color='#6d4aff')\n",
        "        axes[1, 0].axvline(0, color='red', linestyle='--', lw=2)\n",
        "        axes[1, 0].set_xlabel('Residual Value')\n",
        "        axes[1, 0].set_ylabel('Frequency')\n",
        "        axes[1, 0].set_title('Residual Distribution\\n(Normality check)')\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Plot 4: Actual vs Predicted\n",
        "        axes[1, 1].scatter(y_true, y_pred, alpha=0.5, edgecolors='k')\n",
        "        min_val = min(y_true.min(), y_pred.min())\n",
        "        max_val = max(y_true.max(), y_pred.max())\n",
        "        axes[1, 1].plot([min_val, max_val], [min_val, max_val], 'r--', lw=2)\n",
        "        axes[1, 1].set_xlabel('Actual Values')\n",
        "        axes[1, 1].set_ylabel('Predicted Values')\n",
        "        axes[1, 1].set_title('Actual vs Predicted\\n(Linearity check)')\n",
        "\n",
        "        plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "        plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # SUMMARY OUTPUT\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def print_summary(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Print the full statsmodels summary table.\"\"\"\n",
        "        print(self.results.summary())\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    # COEFFICIENT EXTRACTION\n",
        "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "    def get_coefficients(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Return a clean DataFrame of coefficients with statistics.\"\"\"\n",
        "        names = ['const'] + (self.feature_names if self.feature_names \n",
        "                             else [f'x{i}' for i in range(len(self.results.params) - 1)])\n",
        "\n",
        "        coef_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "            'Feature':     names[:len(self.results.params)],\n",
        "            'Coefficient': self.results.params,\n",
        "            'Std_Error':   self.results.bse,\n",
        "            't_value':     self.results.tvalues,\n",
        "            'P_Value':     self.results.pvalues,\n",
        "            'CI_95_Lower': self.results.conf_int()[0],\n",
        "            'CI_95_Upper': self.results.conf_int()[1],\n",
        "            'Significant': ['Yes' if p < 0.05 else 'No' for p in self.results.pvalues]\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        return coef_df"
      ]
    },
    {
