        "---\n",
        "## Part B: Polynomial Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "### Step 4B: Prepare Features and Split\n",
        "\n",
        "Now we use the polynomial dataset with only `age` as predictor. We expect a non-linear relationship, so we'll use `PolynomialFeatures(degree=2)`.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What PolynomialFeatures(degree=2) does:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Given feature `[age]`, it creates: `[age, age²]`\n",
        "\n",
        "Then `add_constant` prepends 1s, giving: `[1, age, age²]`\n",
        "\n",
        "So the model becomes:\n",
        "$$price = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\cdot age + \\beta_2 \\cdot age^2 + \\epsilon$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prepare features and target\n",
        "X_poly = df_poly[['age']]  # Single feature, kept as DataFrame with [[]]\n",
        "y_poly = df_poly['price']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split into train/test\n",
        "X_poly_train, X_poly_test, y_poly_train, y_poly_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X_poly, y_poly, test_size=0.3, random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training set: {len(X_poly_train)} samples\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test set:     {len(X_poly_test)} samples\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
